<div class="topic-sheet">
  <h1>True, False or Not Given - How to answer</h1>
  <section class="summary-block summary-blue">
    <h2>Rules</h2>
    <p><strong>True.</strong> The statement agrees with the passage.</p>
    <p><strong>False.</strong> The statement contradicts the passage. It says the opposite.</p>
    <p><strong>Not given.</strong> The passage does not say enough for you to decide.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="summary-block summary-green">
    <h2>How to answer</h2>
    <p>If the passage and the statement mean the same thing, choose <strong>true</strong>.</p>
    <p>If the passage says the opposite, choose <strong>false</strong>.</p>
    <p>If the passage says nothing, or not enough, choose <strong>not given</strong>.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="summary-block summary-pink">
    <h2>Key tips</h2>
    <p>Do not use outside knowledge. Use only the passage.</p>
    <p>Watch for trap words such as <em>always, never, all</em> and <em>only</em>.</p>
    <p>Be careful with numbers, times and dates.</p>
    <p>If you are guessing or assuming, the answer is usually <strong>not given</strong>.</p>
  </section>
</div>
